; Flavored-borrow DEP spec. The dep OWNS the borrowed types `idx_key` / `idx_plain` (real structs).
;
; `idx_key` contains a field of the Ord-REFUSING extern `opaque` (a hand-written type in the
; generated crate's lib.rs that derives Hash+Eq but deliberately NOT Ord). This makes the Ord
; question compile-observable: under the consumer's `hash` flavor the dep derives only Hash/Eq on
; IdxKey (green — opaque supplies Hash), but widen the borrow to `bare` and IdxKey's derived Ord
; forces `Opaque: Ord`, which fails to compile. That red proof is exactly what the flavor column buys.
;
; `idx_plain` is a plain uint record; a bare borrow makes the dep derive the full Eq/Ord/PartialOrd
; bundle on it. `root` references both so all rules are reachable.
opaque = _CDDL_CODEGEN_EXTERN_TYPE_
idx_key = [h: opaque]
idx_plain = [n: uint]
root = [a: idx_key, b: idx_plain]
